1result.sql is incorrect because it takes MAX(range) from the joined aircrafts_data table. “Range” is the maximum capability of an aircraft, not the length of the flown leg, so the query returns the largest range among planes that ever visited Abakan (~6700 km) instead of the real route distance.

2result.sql, although written as a constant, matches the longest great‑circle leg that actually appears in the data (Abakan ⇆ Grozny, ≈ 3 5 0 6 km) and therefore supplies the right numeric answer, while 1result.sql does not.

```plaintext
2result.sql
```